 },
 "kind": "statement",
 "title": "An ideal is the directed union of its finite type subideals, [stacks-project]",
 "statement": "Let $X$ be qcqs and let $\\mathcal H\\subseteq\\mathcal O_X$ be a quasi-coherent\nideal. The finite type quasi-coherent subideals of $\\mathcal H$ form a family\nwhich is directed under inclusion and whose union is $\\mathcal H$.\n\nSuppose moreover that $U\\subseteq X$ is a quasi-compact open with\n$\\mathcal H|_U=\\mathcal O_U$. Then the subfamily of those finite type\nsubideals $\\mathcal K\\subseteq\\mathcal H$ with $\\mathcal K|_U=\\mathcal O_U$ is\nnonempty, is directed, and still has union $\\mathcal H$; in particular every\nfinite type subideal of $\\mathcal H$ is contained in a member of it.",
 "source": {
  "document": "literature/blueprint/master/blueprint/sec-nagata-compactification/sk-thm-nagata-sketch-conrad/lemma-nagata-ideal-directed-union-finite-type.md",
  "place": "node lemma-nagata-ideal-directed-union-finite-type, order 205"
 },
 "stmt_deps": [
  "def-nagata-extended-ideal"
 ],
 "proof": [
  {
   "text": "The family of finite type subideals is closed under sums, hence directed, and\nits union is contained in $\\mathcal H$. For the reverse inclusion let $V$ be\nan affine open and $a\\in\\mathcal H(V)$. The ideal $\\mathcal J\\subseteq \\mathcal O_V$ generated by $a$ is of finite type and is the restriction of the\nquasi-coherent subideal $\\mathcal J^{\\max}\\cap\\mathcal H\\subseteq\\mathcal H$,\nwhere $\\mathcal J^{\\max}$ is the largest quasi-coherent ideal restricting to\n$\\mathcal J$ on $V$; so\n[lemma-nagata-finite-type-ideal-extension-exists], applied inside\n$\\mathcal H$, produces a finite type $\\mathcal K\\subseteq\\mathcal H$ with\n$\\mathcal K|_V=\\mathcal J$, and then $a\\in\\mathcal K(V)$.",
   "uses": [
    "lemma-nagata-finite-type-ideal-extension-exists"
   ],
   "elementary": false
  },
  {
   "text": "For the second statement, apply\n[lemma-nagata-finite-type-ideal-extension-exists] to $\\mathcal H$ on the\nquasi-compact open $U$, where $\\mathcal H|_U=\\mathcal O_U$ is of finite type:\nit produces a finite type $\\mathcal K'\\subseteq\\mathcal H$ with\n$\\mathcal K'|_U=\\mathcal H|_U=\\mathcal O_U$, so the subfamily is nonempty. It\nis directed because it is again closed under sums. Finally, for any finite\ntype $\\mathcal K\\subseteq\\mathcal H$ the sum $\\mathcal K+\\mathcal K'$ lies in\nthe subfamily and contains $\\mathcal K$, so the subfamily is cofinal in the\nfamily of all finite type subideals and has the same union $\\mathcal H$.",
   "uses": [
    "lemma-nagata-finite-type-ideal-extension-exists"
   ],
   "elementary": false
  }
 ],
